EXPERIMENT 2 – BASICS OF RECONNAISSANCE Passive Information Gathering using WHOIS, NSLOOKUP, DIG and theHarvester AIM To perform passive information gathering of a given domain using WHOIS, NSLOOKUP, DIG and theHarvester. TOOLS REQUIRED Kali Linux Terminal, WHOIS, NSLOOKUP, DIG and theHarvester. PROCEDURE • Open Kali Linux and launch the Terminal. • Execute the WHOIS command to obtain domain registration information. • Execute NSLOOKUP to find the domain's IP addresses. • Execute DIG to retrieve DNS records. • Execute theHarvester using a supported public data source to look for publicly available domain information. • Record the important output of each command. 1. WHOIS Command: whois google.com Output (important details): Domain Name       : GOOGLE.COM Registrar         : MarkMonitor Inc. Creation Date     : 1997-09-15 Expiry Date       : 2028-09-14 Name Server 1     : NS1.GOOGLE.COM Name Server 2     : NS2.GOOGLE.COM Name Server 3     : NS3.GOOGLE.COM Name Server 4     : NS4.GOOGLE.COM DNSSEC            : Unsigned 2. NSLOOKUP Command: nslookup google.com Output: Server   : 192.168.226.2 Address  : 192.168.226.2#53 Name     : google.com Address  : 142.251.43.46 IPv6     : 2404:6800:4007:830::200e 3. DIG Command: dig any google.com Output (important details): Domain Name : google.com Status      : NOERROR A Record    : 142.251.221.174 AAAA Record : 2404:6800:4007:830::200e Name Servers: ns1.google.com Page 1 Experiment 2 – Basics of Reconnaissancens2.google.com ns3.google.com ns4.google.com Query Time  : 140 msec 4. theHarvester Check command: theHarvester -h The help output confirmed that theHarvester version 4.10.1 was installed. The Bing source was not supported in this installed version, so the supported crtsh source was used. Execution command: theHarvester -d google.com -b crtsh -l 100 Output: Target          : google.com Search Source   : CRTsh IPs Found       : 0 Emails Found    : 0 People Found    : 0 Hosts Found     : 0 Note: The selected CRTsh source returned no results in this run. This is recorded as the actual observed output; it does not mean that the domain has no publicly available information. RESULT Passive information gathering was performed for the domain google.com using WHOIS, NSLOOKUP, DIG and theHarvester. The domain registration details and DNS information were obtained, and theHarvester completed the query with no results returned by the selected CRTsh source. Page 2 Experiment 2 – Basics of Reconnaissance
